    "body": "Audit of #692 on main bdd29e00 (after #705 and #709), issue-worker-high.\n\n| Point (body / Done means) | Status | Pinned by / bypassing call site |\n|---|---|---|\n| Shared feature graph + pick API in app | met | `app::pick::{feature_graph, feature_pick, feature_sel}` |\n| Flat-face triangulation edges not pickable | met | `feature_pick::flat_face_triangulation_edges_are_not_pickable`; UI `one_pick_rule::a_click_on_a_flat_faces_diagonal_picks_the_face_never_an_edge` |\n| Cylinder facet edges not pickable, rim is | met | `feature_pick::cylinder_facet_edges_are_not_pickable_but_its_rim_is`; UI `one_pick_rule::a_smooth_walls_facet_seam_is_no_edge` |\n| Box corner is a point, face-interior vertex is not | met | `feature_pick::a_box_corner_is_a_point_but_a_vertex_inside_a_face_is_not`; UI `one_pick_rule::a_box_corner_picks_as_a_point_where_points_are_taken` |\n| Far-side edge not picked through, perspective and ortho | met | `feature_pick::a_far_side_edge_is_not_picked_through_the_near_face`; UI `one_pick_rule::a_click_over_a_hidden_edge_takes_the_near_face_or_nothing_never_the_edge` |\n| Pick-through, when on, picks it | met (API) | `feature_pick::pick_through_does_pick_the_far_side_edge`. The UI offers no pick-through mode (`feature_click::query_at` always sends `through: false`), so nothing on the far side is ever picked from the viewport |\n| Snap order point > edge > face, only kinds the tool takes | met | `feature_click::ask`; `one_pick_rule::a_box_corner_picks_as_a_point_where_points_are_taken` (Edge mode never snaps to a point), `feature_pick_wire::a_pick_resolves_to_the_selection_its_page_stores` |\n| Degenerate input: nothing pickable, no panic | met | `feature_pick::degenerate_input_picks_nothing_and_never_panics` |\n| Every UI picker on the rule: op geometry, boundary, plane, axis, three points, fixture locate, WCS chips, hover | met | all Face/Edge/Vertex clicks and hovers go through `ui::feature_click` -> `pick::pick_selection`; UI tests `one_pick_rule::*` (op page, Setups axis rows, fixture locate draft, three points). The \"fixture locate wires once #566 merges\" note is out of date: `locate_and_points_drafts_take_box_corners_as_points` pins it |\n| Probe op from a picked feature | met | reads the stored picks (`operation::probe_from_picks`), which only the rule (GUI) or `mcp::pick::picks_of` (MCP, `check_pickable`) can store |\n| MCP picks: list_features, set_operation_geometry, area, set_part_axes, lay_part_on_points | met | `mcp::pick::pick_of` -> `pick::check_pickable`; `mcp_pick::listed_chains_and_vertices_follow_the_one_pick_rule`, `feature_pick_wire::a_pick_by_id_must_be_one_a_click_could_make` |\n| MCP `locate_part` (fixture locate mates, #561) | **not met** | `mcp/fixture_tools.rs` `locate_part` parses the mate ids with `parse_feature_id` and skips `check_pickable`: a vertex along a round rim or inside a face is taken as a mate point |\n| Circle/arc centre picks (`PickKinds::CENTRES`) | waits for #759 | the API has the centre tier; no page asks for it until the WCS circle-centre PR (#759, draft) lands |\n| Model-mode entity click and hover | not a feature pick | `interact::pick_model` / `update_hover` use `pick::first_hit_f`, the app's front-most-surface law (models over stock); they select a whole model, never a face, edge or point |\n| WCS anchor grid (`interact::anchor_hit`) | not a model pick | the nine stock/model-box anchor markers, drawn on top; no geometry is picked |\n| User docs note on what a click picks | **not met** | nothing in `site/content/guide/` |\n\nPlan: route `locate_part` through `check_pickable` (pinned by an MCP test), add the user-guide note, decision record. Draft PR follows.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
